+# Callback registration and its returned pair
+
+The target is the complete 132-byte function at RVA `0x0083F1C0`, with
+`ret 8` on both exits and no branch outside its extent. The existing evidence
+in `0083f1c0-bfme2-callback-retry.md` establishes the callback payload, receiver
+fields and failure-reporting imports. Its requested reopening condition is
+now met: Open-BFME-2 at `d8dcd30e0cda47386f50b031c2bbcc8b9910cc02` contains a
+verified `ios_base::register_callback` in
+`Code/Libraries/Source/WWVegas/WWLib/stlport_ios_base_iword.cpp`, at target RVA
+`0x0001C090`. Its evidence is
+`reverse/attempt_support/ios-callback-local-count-20261021/readme.md`.
+
+An independent comparison of the two retail images finds the same 48
+instructions over 132 bytes. Only the grow call, imported `_iob`, literal
+`ios failure` and imported `fputs` operands differ. The 147-byte grow bodies
+at BFME1 `0x0083EF20` and BFME2 `0x0001BEC0` likewise have the same 60
+instructions, differing only in the `realloc` import address. The two existing
+117-byte BFME1 iword/pword bodies have the same instruction sequences as their
+BFME2 counterparts, with the expected target-specific bindings.
+
+The source hypothesis uses the actual vendored `ios_base` and
+`pair<event_callback, int>` definitions. The pair returned by the grow helper
+is non-POD, so C++ supplies its hidden return-storage argument. This recovers
+the native call shape without an explicit output-pointer declaration. The
+donor shows why this distinction matters: the old declaration yields the
+same helper bytes but chooses the wrong stderr register in its caller.
+The target callback layout and uses are established independently above;
+the original helper spelling is not established. `grow_array` remains the
+existing recovery's spelling, with its return and payload types corrected.
+
+The existing helper identity at `0x0083EF20` is:
+
+```
+??$grow_array@UCallback@_STL@@@_STL@@YAPAU?$GrowPair@UCallback@_STL@@@0@PAU10@PAUCallback@0@II@Z
+```
+
+Its proposed replacement compiled identity is:
+
+```
+??$grow_array@U?$pair@P6AXW4event@ios_base@_STL@@AAV23@H@ZH@_STL@@@_STL@@YA?AU?$pair@PAU?$pair@P6AXW4event@ios_base@_STL@@AAV23@H@ZH@_STL@@I@0@PAU?$pair@P6AXW4event@ios_base@_STL@@AAV23@H@ZH@0@II@Z
+```
+
+BFME1 has no ICF allowance. If native qualification succeeds, replace this
+one helper owner through normal `add_match --correct-identity`, rather than
+adding the second identity used by the BFME2 donor. Its old standalone source
+must then be removed. The two existing fallback data cells retain their
+names, sizes and source owner. Leave the generated ASM file unchanged, as
+required for a converted row.
+
+Use BFME1's own vendored headers. Their version macro is `0x460`; the donor's
+is `0x452`. The relevant pair constructors and callback layout agree, but
+this is not a substitute for native BFME1 compilation. Ordinary admission
+must verify all four bodies, the two data rows, imports and relocations.
+The new recovery can credit only the 132 callback bytes; rehoming the existing
+147-byte helper and retaining the two 117-byte wrappers add no coverage.
